651 :             Pointer pointer = (Pointer) iterator.next();
652 :             list.add(pointer.getNode());
653 :         }
654 :         return list;
655 :     }
```
This method collects nodes in the order produced by the iterator but does not sort them.

The important method is `DOMNodePointer.compareChildNodePointers` which compares two child nodes according to document order using DOM node relationships:
```java
